    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d677">

                <pb facs="0820" n="534" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg534"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/7074d</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 25, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2779. Your 3636, 24th. It is not desired that British Government issue permits
                    for amount sugar-beet seed in excess of existing permits. <pb facs="0821"
                        n="535" xml:id="pg535"/> On contrary, owing German and Austrian embargoes,
                    seed now coming forward or to be brought forward this season will net total
                    one-half of the 140,000 [140,300] bags for which permits granted, and probably
                    much less than one-half. Substitute permits desired for shipments specified in
                    Department’s 2698<anchor n="1" xml:id="d677-f1"/> and 2748 because some of
                    ultimate recipients had not obtained permits. These are Edward
                        Starke 2,200 bags, Jacob Savageau 1,800
                    bags, A. Bencoe 1,200 bags, DeRekowski
                    3,000 bags, and Winterhalter 3,200 bags.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
